  "limitations": [
    "The paper contains logical inconsistencies in the interpretation of statistical p-values, particularly in the 'p-value' section (p. 10-11), which may affect the validity of its conclusions.",
    "There are discrepancies in reported coefficients for the 'Success' variable across different tables and textual descriptions (e.g., Table 7 vs. regression equation text vs. Figure 3)."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This empirical study develops and tests a Human Resource Management (HRM) model with ICT architecture for the Android operating environment. The system aims to simplify firm administration, streamline corporate processes, and reduce human resource requirements. Functional tests showed high success rates across modules, with most achieving 100% and the training module achieving 99%. The overall system demonstrated an almost 100% transaction success rate and a reaction time of less than 1.5 seconds. Regression analysis indicated that variables like Success, Fail, and Failure rate could explain a very high percentage (99.99%) of the variance in the number of usage occurrences. However, the paper contains significant inconsistencies in its statistical reporting and interpretation, particularly regarding p-values and regression coefficients, which are a notable limitation.",
